WEBVTT

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.370
It was on a Sunday, in November...

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.700
Here you are.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.040
T-thanks.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.040
So you're telling me that after your
friend Ouija-boarded in the classroom,

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.380
she has been acting strangely?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.710
Yes.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:34.380
She'd jump up onto her
desk during class time,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.050
and eat sand from
the sandbox during gym.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:43.060
So, I was thinking that maybe
she had been possessed by a fox.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:55.740
Why am I not good enough?

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.740
Answer me.

00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.740
I'll be all that you...

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:07.250
You should take your friend
to the hospital.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:10.250
H-hold on, Naru!

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:49.850
You might have said it some other way!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.190
I thought it fell under
a doctor's purview.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.520
That's all I was saying.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.530
You could at least refer her
to someone, or something!

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.530
Hey, guys!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.700
Naru-chan, yoo-hoo!

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.200
W-who's that?

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.870
Man, Shibuya is no place
to come on a Sunday.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:12.210
Oh, Mai-chan, an ice coffee, please.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.040
M-Monk? What's with the outfit?

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:18.880
Oh, this? I had a live show today.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:21.380
I'm always performing
in basement studios,

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:23.720
so it feels nice to be in front
of people after all this time,

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.220
but it is exhausting.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.230
Monk, you were in a band!?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.560
No, I wasn't in a band,
it's my real job.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.570
I'm a professional bassist.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:38.900
T-then, you're a monk on the side?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.900
What about being at Mt. Koya?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.570
I was. It's my family's temple,

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:46.240
and my pop wanted me to be a monk.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.910
But you can't bring CDs and stuff
up on the mountain, so I left.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:56.920
Still, in this profession, there's
a surprising amount of curses and such.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.260
Being an ex-monk, whenever
something comes up, I get called in,

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.340
so I have a side business
as a prayersmith. Got it?

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.600
Uh-huh... got it...

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.930
I guess you can't judge someone
by appearances.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:15.270
Well, in Monk's case, it's him actually
being a monk that smells fishy.

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.610
So, what is your business here today?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:25.950
Oh, yeah, I actually
am here on business.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.620
I'd like to make use of a bit
of your knowledge, Naru-chan.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:33.620
There's a student from a high school
here in the city who follows our band,

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:37.290
and she came and talked
to me after our show today.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.960
Norio, you can perform exorcisms, right?

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.960
Huh? Yeah.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:51.640
So, from what she tells me, there's
a seat in her class that is cursed.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:54.890
Anyone who has sat in this
seat over the last three months

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.650
seems to get into accidents,
one after the next.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:00.320
And they're all under
the exact same circumstances.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.490
They've all gotten dragged
off by trains,

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.490
with their arms caught in the door.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:10.330
There have been four people who have
sat in that seat since September.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:14.330
All of them have had accidents.
One got off easy,

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.670
but the other three
were seriously hurt.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:21.340
And that's not all. Her teacher
made a fuss about seeing ghosts,

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.010
and was hospitalized.
Even now, he keeps coughing up blood

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.340
for no explainable reason.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:28.340
There are loads of other
strange incidents

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.680
and accidents coming out of that school,

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.350
and I hear there's even someone
they say has been possessed.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.690
Possessed?

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:39.360
So, I was thinking that maybe
she had been possessed by a fox.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:44.360
Monk, was the school that the girl
asked you about Yuasa High School?

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.360
That's right. You know about it?

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:51.030
Um, may I come in?

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.370
Yes. Do you have an inquiry?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.500
This is who I am.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.210
"Mikami Noboru, Principal,
Yuasa Private High School"
This is who I am.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.370
This is who I am.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.380
Yuasa High School!?

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.060
"Principal's Office"

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:21.480
"Principal's Office"
Thank you for coming over.

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:22.400
Thank you for coming over.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:25.400
This is Yoshino-sensei,
one of our guidance counselors.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.740
He will show you around the school.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:31.070
Pleasure... to meet you.

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:33.740
You said you wanted
a room made ready,

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.080
so we cleared a small
conference room for you.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.420
We've told anyone who needs
to speak to you to see you there.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.750
So this is our base this time, is it?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.090
Let's bring in
the equipment at once.

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:48.090
Lin...

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.430
Right.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.430
Um, are you the leader here?

00:06:52.430 --> 00:06:54.760
Oh, no, he is.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:56.430
Something wrong?

00:06:56.430 --> 00:06:59.440
Er, you see...

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.770
Before the students come by,

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:05.190
there's something...
I'd like to discuss.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.910
I'm listening. Please, have a seat.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:17.290
Well, you see...
at night I, um...

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.790
hear this knocking sound.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:29.300
It just won't let up, so when I went
ahead and opened the curtain...

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:37.140
Lately, as a result of that,
I haven't been able to sleep.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:40.810
Has there been anyone else in your
family that has heard the sounds?

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.890
Yes.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:45.150
But it doesn't seem to be bothering
them as much as it does me.

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.230
I see.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:56.490
Ito Kiyomi-san, wasn't it?

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.830
Yes.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.160
At the office, you told
me that you thought

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:03.500
your friend had been
possessed by a fox.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:04.500
How is she today?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:07.170
She's been staying home for a while.

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.920
You said that she jumped on
the desk, and was eating sand.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.930
That's not all.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:17.390
One time, she dove into the pool,
wearing her uniform.

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.850
It was awfully cold that day, too.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.190
Has she done any harm to others?

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.520
No, none of that.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:27.860
I would think that usually,
when someone was in such a state,

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.190
one would wonder if they weren't ill.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.530
Why did you think she was
possessed by a fox?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:37.530
Well, she said "I am the white fox,
messenger of the harvest god."

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:40.200
She started acting strange
after the Ouija-boarding.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.870
When it was time to go home,

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:45.210
she'd suddenly say she thought
she was being possessed.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.540
I told her she couldn't be, but
she said her shoulders were heavy.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:51.050
Beginning the next day,
she acted strange.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.890
Where was it that you
were Ouija-boarding?

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:58.550
Classroom 1-3.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:01.560
The track team's room is all weird.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:02.890
The lockers fall over,

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:05.560
and the equipment gets scattered about.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.900
We thought someone was playing a joke,

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.570
so we all stayed over in the room,
to keep watch,

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.570
but when we looked away
for just a minute,

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:17.570
the shots that had been put away
in a box were all lined up on the floor.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.580
There's this storage room in the gym,

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.910
and ever since last month,
when we did a test of nerve in there,

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.250
I've been seeing these strange shadows.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.580
One of the girls I did it with said that

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.580
she's seeing ghosts coming
out of her desk, too.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.590
Her desk?

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:34.590
Yes. Um... During class,
she suddenly couldn't move,

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.260
and she felt like someone was
touching her around her tummy,

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.590
and when she looked...

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:44.930
She said it's happened many times.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:49.770
Then, she got an ulcer,
and had to go to the hospital.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.440
Excuse me.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:58.280
Norio! You really did come!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:01.280
Yeah. Let me introduce you.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.950
The handsome one over here is Shibuya,

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.620
the manager of Shibuya Psychic Research,

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.920
and the young lady there
is his assistant, Taniyama.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:12.630
I'm Takahashi Yuko. Nice to meet you.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.960
Hello.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:16.300
So, what's with the "Norio"?

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.630
That's what they call me in the band.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.800
My real name is Hosho, right?

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.640
- So...
- Getting right to it,

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.140
this is the girl who sat at the desk,

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:27.980
and had the accident with the train?

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.650
Yes.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:31.980
I was the second one.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.980
I got off the train,
and started walking,

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.650
when suddenly, my arm was being pulled,
and got caught in the doors.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.660
Then, the train started to leave,
and I was dragged along like that.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.990
The train stopped right away,
but my shoulder was dislocated,

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.660
and my legs came away like this.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.330
Was there anyone near
the door at the time?

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.830
Mm-mm, no one.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.170
It had just emptied out,
and there weren't many people,

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.000
so I had a clear view.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:59.680
Any idea why there would be any strange
occurrences surrounding that seat?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:01.800
None, huh?

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.810
I'd like to see this seat.

00:11:05.010 --> 00:11:07.270
Well, I'll take you to it.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.690
Over there.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.860
Anyone here now?

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:18.690
No, nobody.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.530
The girl who was here last
got seriously hurt,

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.030
and she's in the hospital.

00:11:22.030 --> 00:11:24.030
The desk's location hasn't changed?

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:26.370
Mm-hmm, it's always been here.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.710
Oh, you took your time!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.050
What's going on at this school!?

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:47.060
With everything that's here,
who's going to exorcise it all?

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:52.060
Me? Am I? I'm going to cry here...

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.400
Sorry I can't be any help.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:58.400
This isn't normal.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.740
Individually, these cases
aren't a big deal,

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.070
but this many of them is abnormal.

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:07.080
This many cases, in the same place,
at the same time...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.750
Assuming they're all true,

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.500
there definitely has
to be something causing it.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:16.750
It's true, there are too
many cases here.

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:30.100
What exactly is going
on at this school?

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:41.110
In any case, with this many of them,
we can't investigate slowly.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:44.780
I think all we can do is exorcise
anything that comes our way.

00:12:44.780 --> 00:12:48.450
If that doesn't work, then we'll
figure out what to do after that.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.460
Hara-san, please look around the school.

00:12:53.460 --> 00:12:55.790
Start with the desk they say
that spirits appear from,

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.460
and the track team's room.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.800
I wouldn't mind at all if you
were to just call me Masako.

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.800
Ooh, how galling!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:08.140
Matsuzaki-san, please go with her.
If there are any spirits, exorcise them.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.100
Oh?

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.470
Aren't you going to say
anything back to Masako?

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:17.150
I seem to remember having something
quite awful said to me before.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:19.820
If you have the time to go on
about such extraneous matters,

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:23.490
I'd rather have you display
your talents of exorcism.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:27.820
Matsuzaki-san, I would like
to see you in action, eventually.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:33.160
There are so many cases this time,
I don't have enough equipment.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.830
You'll have to rely on your
own spiritual sensitivity.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:37.830
You too, Monk and John.

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.830
You got it.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:40.840
Understood.

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.170
Lin and I will continue investigating.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:45.840
Mai, you wait here, and wait
for everyone to contact you.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:46.840
Roger.

00:13:46.840 --> 00:13:49.180
All right, let's begin.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:57.810
"Track team"

00:14:04.190 --> 00:14:06.700
Not too much difference
from the air outside.

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:11.530
Here I end up being
the only one left out.

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:15.200
Not much I can do about it though,

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.540
since I don't have any powers
of exorcism, like the others.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.170
If I did have them,
I'm sure that even Naru would-

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.210
Y-you startled me!

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:28.550
Sorry, sorry. I thought
maybe Norio was in here.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.890
What are you doing?

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.890
I'm holding things down here.
Monk is out on patrol.

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:37.230
So, is the exorcism coming along?

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:40.230
We just barely got started.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.230
But it looks like it'll
be a lot of trouble.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.020
There are so many of them here.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:49.240
There sure are. Good grief,
what is going on at this school?

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.240
Curses, and ghosts,
and supernatural powers...

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:53.910
All we need now is for a UFO to appear-

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.750
J-just a minute. Supernatural powers?

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.250
The Kasai Panic?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.920
Yes. There's this girl in 3rd Year
named Kasai Chiaki-san,

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.930
and she could bend spoons
using supernatural powers.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.430
It was just after summer
vacation was over, I think.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.260
She became famous all over school,
just like that.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:17.930
Thanks to her, spoon-bending
became this whole scene.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:21.270
The school got divided up into
believers and non-believers,

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.270
and there was a big fuss about it.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.270
Kasai-san got hauled up in front

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.280
of the whole school during
morning assembly.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:29.610
If it's true, then try bending this.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.450
Can you do that? You can't can you?

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:36.290
She bent it?

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:39.040
After that, it was a real mess.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:41.580
A faction of the teachers
launched this concentrated attack.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:47.090
Obviously, it's some trick!
Stop making fools of other people!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.630
So, Kasai-san finally snapped,
and told the teachers,

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.300
I'll curse you to death!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:58.720
And that's when all the stories
of weird things happening started up.

00:15:58.970 --> 00:16:04.310
Now, everyone's saying that maybe
this is all the curse of Kasai-san.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:07.980
I think that's why lately,
Kasai-san hasn't even come to class,

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:08.190
and she spends all her time holed
up in the biology prep room.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.530
"Biology Prep Room"
and she spends all her time holed
up in the biology prep room.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.320
And she spends all her time holed
up in the biology prep room.

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.330
Yes?

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:20.000
Excuse me, is Kasai-san in here?

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.460
What is this concerning?

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:25.330
My name is Shibuya,
from Shibuya Psychic Research.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:28.670
I would like to speak with Kasai-san.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:31.670
I'm sorry, what was your name again?

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.680
My name is Shibuya Kazuya.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:38.680
Ah, I'd heard from the principal
that someone was coming to investigate,

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.180
so you're him.

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:42.180
Please, come in.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:46.360
I teach biology here.
My name is Ubusuna Kei.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:50.030
Ubusuna? That's an unusual name.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:56.240
Kasai-san? Then, this is about
the incident in September?

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:59.030
I don't have anything to say!
Leave me alone!

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.370
You'd better tell them
exactly what happened,

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:03.040
to avoid any misunderstandings.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:07.380
No! He's just going
to call me a liar, too!

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:11.380
But he investigates psychic phenomena.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:16.050
He's not going to categorically
reject what you say.

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.600
What is it you want to ask me?

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:23.390
I have heard that perhaps
you are the reason

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:28.060
for the outbreak of mysterious
events here at this school.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:31.400
Stories that you have bent spoons and
keys with supernatural powers, as well.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.740
They're not stories,
they're the truth,

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:36.660
but you don't believe in
supernatural powers, do you?

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:41.740
Why not? Even I am able to
do as much as bend a spoon.

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.080
You can?

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:49.080
I can. There aren't any psychic
researchers that don't believe in PK.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:54.090
Show me.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:57.090
I guess I have no choice.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.440
I was watching this late-night
show during summer vacation.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:17.110
They were doing spoon-bending on it.

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:20.120
So, while I was trying to imitate
more or less what they were doing,

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:24.450
I got so I could bend them. I can't
break them, like you can, though.

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.790
It's been three months.
Can you still do it?

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:28.960
Sure I can!

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.810
No, don't do that!

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:50.480
You were about to bend the spoon
against the edge of the chair, right?

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.150
If anyone ever caught you
using tricks like that,

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:54.400
no one would believe you anymore.

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:57.490
That's not true! I really can do it!

00:18:57.490 --> 00:19:00.160
Any researcher knows that
the power of someone

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.830
with psychic abilities can be
unstable when affected by others.

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:07.160
When you can't do it,
it's okay to just say so.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:10.830
The people who don't believe you weren't
going to believe you to begin with,

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.170
so you can ignore them.

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:13.840
That's easy to say,

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.510
but you don't know what people will
say to you if you can't do it, do you?

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:19.170
Kei-sensei stood up for me,

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:22.180
and now the other teachers
look at her with disgust.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.510
Never mind about me.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:29.690
I felt sorry for her, what with
everyone rejecting her like they did.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:33.190
But the other biology club
members quit, saying things like,

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:35.190
"What are they doing in that club?"

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.530
Why do I have to go through
this sort of thing!?

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.530
That's why you said those words.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.200
I'll curse you to death!

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:44.870
Oh, no. I might have said that,

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:48.290
but I couldn't really curse
them to death, could I?

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:49.870
Right?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.880
I kind of feel sorry for Kasai-san.

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:02.220
Having this big an uproar being made,
just over bending spoons.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:09.890
Mai, I need a favor.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:11.560
A-a favor?

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:15.900
Please keep that spoon-bending I did
earlier a secret from the others.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.570
Especially Lin.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:21.900
I-I'd like to ask him why, but...

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.990
Sure thing. I won't tell them. I promise.

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:30.250
Thanks.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:33.580
Is this the first secret
that just me and Naru share?

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.000
No, that can't be!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:38.250
It's the truth.
There are no spirits here.

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:41.920
I looked all over the school,
but there aren't any anywhere.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:44.930
There has to at least be one
in that seat, right?

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:47.260
There were four accidents
in a row from there!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.100
We are being deceived.

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:52.770
By everyone in the whole school?

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:54.270
You've got to be kidding me!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.270
Now, now...

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.270
Masako may not necessarily be correct.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:02.610
I still think I'm more correct
than you are, Matsuzaki-san.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:03.280
Huh!?

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.610
Matsuzaki-san, I wonder
if you have ever had an instance

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.280
where what you said was correct.

00:21:07.280 --> 00:21:09.450
Well, I never! You may see them,
but you can't exorcise them!

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:11.620
Lin, let's get back to work.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.620
Right.

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:16.290
Let's go take another
lap around, ourselves.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:18.630
You bet.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:20.630
Make sure you look closely this time.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:22.710
No matter how much I look,
it'll be the same.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:29.300
And I'm staying here again.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:31.640
No spirits, huh?

00:21:31.640 --> 00:21:35.640
But if there aren't any,
why are there so many incidents?

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:38.310
No, no!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.480
What would Naru say to me
if he caught me napping!?

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.670
Naru...

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.010
Foxfires.

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:07.090
Foxfires?

00:23:43.440 --> 00:23:48.440
Next time: File 3,
"The After School Hexer" #2
